==German==

===Alternative spellings===
* {{qualifier|Swiss Standard German}} [[stossen]]

===Etymology===
{{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|stōzan}}. Akin to Old Norse {{term|stauta|lang=non}} and {{term|steyta|lang=non}} ( > Danish {{term|støde|lang=da}}), Gothic {{term|𐍃𐍄𐌰𐌿𐍄𐌰𐌽|tr=stautan|lang=got}}. Non-Germanic cognates include Latin {{term|tundo|lang=la}}. Cf. Sanskrit {{term|तुदति||tr=tudati|to strike, goad|lang=sa}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/'ʃtoːsən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-stoßen.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{transitive}} to [[push]]; to [[shove]]; to [[thrust]]
# {{transitive|or|reflexive}} to [[bump]]; to [[knock]]; to [[strike]]; to [[hurt]]
# {{reflexive|figurative|with “[[an#German|an]] ...”|lang=de}} to [[take exception]] (to something)
# {{intransitive}} to [[jolt]]; to [[kick]]; to [[thrust]]

